1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:01,778
Do you know why, in English,

2
00:00:01,778 --> 00:00:04,000
we sometimes use A, and sometimes THE?

3
00:00:04,000 --> 00:00:07,000
For the answer, let’s visit England a thousand years ago!

4
00:00:07,000 --> 00:00:08,778
In 1066, the king of England

5
00:00:08,778 --> 00:00:11,000
dies without an heir.

6
00:00:11,000 --> 00:00:13,546
Now England needs a king:

7
00:00:13,546 --> 00:00:15,000
England needs a king.

8
00:00:15,000 --> 00:00:16,636
But there’s a problem: three men

9
00:00:16,636 --> 00:00:18,000
each want the throne!

10
00:00:18,000 --> 00:00:21,000
First, Harold is crowned.

11
00:00:21,000 --> 00:00:24,000
But the king of Norway invades!

12
00:00:24,000 --> 00:00:25,333
Harold defeats him,

13
00:00:25,333 --> 00:00:28,000
but before he can catch his breath,

14
00:00:28,000 --> 00:00:32,000
William arrives with another army!

15
00:00:32,000 --> 00:00:33,875
This time, Harold is killed

16
00:00:33,875 --> 00:00:35,000
and William becomes:

17
00:00:35,000 --> 00:00:39,000
The king of England!

18
00:00:39,000 --> 00:00:40,500
Notice? First we said A KING:

19
00:00:40,500 --> 00:00:42,000
a king—we haven’t specified which one.

20
00:00:42,000 --> 00:00:45,000
But THE KING means that particular king!

21
00:00:45,000 --> 00:00:46,333
Interestingly, the roots of this distinction

22
00:00:46,333 --> 00:00:47,222
go back to Old English!

23
00:00:47,222 --> 00:00:49,000
A comes from ĀN, meaning “one.”

24
00:00:49,000 --> 00:00:51,692
THE belongs to the demonstrative family, like “that”:

25
00:00:51,692 --> 00:00:54,000
something like “that one” or “the very one.”

26
00:00:54,000 --> 00:00:55,500
So what’s the key difference?

27
00:00:55,500 --> 00:00:58,875
When your listener can identify exactly which thing you mean,

28
00:00:58,875 --> 00:01:00,000
we usually use THE;

29
00:01:00,000 --> 00:01:04,000
even if it hasn’t been mentioned before!

30
00:01:04,000 --> 00:01:05,538
To practise this distinction,

31
00:01:05,538 --> 00:01:09,000
we’ve prepared a visual challenge and a practical worksheet.

32
00:01:09,000 --> 00:01:11,340
Just comment THE

33
00:01:11,340 --> 00:01:12,744
and we’ll send them to you!
